From: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:38:58 -0700
Subject: [gl] CHECK glGenTextures does not return 0

If glGenTextures fails, it can be due to exhaustion of resources.
CHECK such failures as GPU process is in stalemate regardless as
texture creation does not work anymore.

Bug: 568891853
Change-Id: Ibb9e0f61064beca6f203a32a8f4e7e30114539d5
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8664215
Reviewed-by: Vasiliy Telezhnikov <vasilyt@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729233}

diff --git a/ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.cc b/ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.cc
index 6e785fafa2c382cfd93dd74647d6a9dbc823c4d5..d5eeeafba9ff5f36b6cf3e27ff7c6bf5128900fe 100644
--- a/ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/gl_gl_api_implementation.cc
@@ -261,6 +261,13 @@ const GLubyte* RealGLApi::glGetStringiFn(GLenum name, GLuint index) {
   return GLApiBase::glGetStringiFn(name, index);
 }
 
+void RealGLApi::glGenTexturesFn(GLsizei n, GLuint* textures) {
+  GLApiBase::glGenTexturesFn(n, textures);
+  if (GetGLImplementation() != kGLImplementationMockGL && n > 0) {
+    CHECK_NE(UNSAFE_TODO(textures[0]), 0u);
+  }
+}
+
 void RealGLApi::glTexImage2DFn(GLenum target,
                                GLint level,
                                GLint internalformat,
